essay_justifications = {
    "M2L2-E01": "For x=-2 the condition x>0 is false, so its indented body is skipped; for x=5 it is true. The unindented Done statement is outside the conditional body and therefore runs in both cases.",
    "M2L2-E02": "The two greater-than tests cover the unequal cases. For comparable numeric inputs, if neither x>y nor y>x is true, the values must be equal, so the final else is valid.",
    "M2L2-E03": "A year is a leap year when it is divisible by 400, or divisible by 4 but not by 100. Thus 2000 meets the 400 exception, 1900 is excluded by the century rule, 2024 qualifies, and 2023 does not divide by 4.",
    "M2L2-E04": "An if/elif chain stops after its first true branch. Since 12>0 is already true, testing it first prevents the later 12>10 branch from being reached; checking the narrower threshold first preserves both outcomes.",
    "M2L2-E05": "Eligibility requires both inclusive comparisons to be true. The conjunction rejects age 20 and income 24,999, while equality at either threshold qualifies when the other condition also passes.",
    "M2L2-E06": "The rates are selected by the first matching tariff branch and each bill is units multiplied by that rate. Failure of earlier upper-bound tests establishes the implicit lower bound of each later band.",
    "M2L2-E07": "The ordered conditions separate sign and parity, with zero handled explicitly. Each input matches its sign/parity combination; the final else covers the remaining negative odd case after the earlier branches fail.",
    "M2L2-E08": "The chain preserves the original three mutually exclusive outcomes while removing one nesting level. With x=4 and y=9, equality is false and x<y is true, so result is 'x less'.",
}
for essay in essays:
    essay["justification"] = essay_justifications[essay["id"]]

